Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[" Exercises 5.8   ", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"74ce76e0-29ba-446c-b4a6-3d231c4e68a4"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\t5.8.1", "Section",
 FontSize->18,ExpressionUUID->"640d7e5b-7407-4bab-b3f3-9de94770b47d"],

Cell["\<\
In deriving equation 5.10, why is it that the density \[Rho] of a substance \
and not its mass appears?\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6f915fc9-472f-4b05-9746-d8f0c8ff0575"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\t5.8.7", "Section",
 FontSize->18,ExpressionUUID->"77ab14ca-9f1f-4034-aa91-a7da48cb9ded"],

Cell["\<\
Find the steady-state solution to equation 5.37 using boundary conditions \
5.34 and 5.38 (and also equation 5.29).  Specifically, find the exact \
solutions (not the numerical solutions).

Next, plot the steady-state solutions corresponding to both the pollution \
density and oxygen concentration using the values used in class (note that \
\[Gamma] = 2).

Finally, interpret the results.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b72f39c0-e8e4-4461-b950-4b7fdb3bfee1"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Predator-prey\nLogistic limited growth\n\
Reaction-diffusion equations:",
 FontSize->18]], "Section",ExpressionUUID->"347a7956-6459-4ce3-90d4-\
7199f8ca59d2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Recall our plankton distribution on the surface of the ocean.  If a new \
element is introduced in terms of a predator, a tiny crustacean called a \
copepod, which consumes the plankton, then we have a predator-prey problem.\n\
\nWe will create a conservation based PDE model for both the predator and the \
prey.  The flux term for the plankton will assumed to be by diffusion only.  \
Likewise, the flux term for the tiny crustacean is also by diffusion only.  \
Although the crustacean has a higher diffusion coefficient due to the \
increased mobility of the crustacean over the plankton.\n\n\tLet  \[Rho][x,t] \
 =  plankton concentration\n\n",
 StyleBox["\t",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", "\[Rho]", ")"}]}], "  ", "==", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"-", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x"], " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", " ", "\[Mu]"}], "*", 
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x"], " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", "\[Rho]", ")"}]}]}], ")"}]}]}], "   ", "+", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"k1", "[", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Rho]", ",", "h"}], "]"}]}]}]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"b4b137af-8653-49d3-be82-b1e23fd702bf"],
 StyleBox["\n\t",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", "\[Rho]", ")"}]}], "  ", "==", "   ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "*", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
       RowBox[{"x", ",", "x"}]], " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", "\[Rho]", ")"}]}]}], "   ", "+", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"k1", "[", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Rho]", ",", "h"}], "]"}]}]}]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"87d2e312-cacf-4148-b6cc-66dffd9f73c4"],
 StyleBox["\n\t",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", 
      RowBox[{"x", ",", "t"}], "]"}], ")"}]}], "  ", "==", "   ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "*", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
       RowBox[{"x", ",", "x"}]], " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", 
        RowBox[{"x", ",", "t"}], "]"}], ")"}]}]}], "   ", "+", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"k1", "[", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", 
       RowBox[{"x", ",", "t"}], "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"h", "[", 
       RowBox[{"x", ",", "t"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"09ea5897-bf7d-4fb3-9ab2-1d8703dcb44a"],
 "\n \n\tLet  h[x,t]  =  crustacean concentration\n\n",
 StyleBox["  \t",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", "h", ")"}]}], "  ", "==", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"-", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x"], " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", " ", "\[Nu]"}], "*", 
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x"], " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", "h", ")"}]}]}], ")"}]}]}], "   ", "+", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"k2", "[", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Rho]", ",", "h"}], "]"}]}]}]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"dac48444-7561-4d5c-a92d-c36a12b5cdd9"],
 StyleBox["\n \t",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", "h", ")"}]}], "  ", "==", "   ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[Nu]", "*", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
       RowBox[{"x", ",", "x"}]], " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", "h", ")"}]}]}], "   ", "+", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"k2", "[", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Rho]", ",", "h"}], "]"}]}]}]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"f2acad31-31af-4065-8b6e-af900dfd00e4"],
 StyleBox["\n \t",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"h", "[", 
      RowBox[{"x", ",", "t"}], "]"}], ")"}]}], "  ", "==", "   ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[Nu]", "*", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
       RowBox[{"x", ",", "x"}]], " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"h", "[", 
        RowBox[{"x", ",", "t"}], "]"}], ")"}]}]}], "   ", "+", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"k2", "[", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", 
       RowBox[{"x", ",", "t"}], "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"h", "[", 
       RowBox[{"x", ",", "t"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"a161d21b-f1a7-4306-a07f-2fc03b64c35a"],
 "\n"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"88fbbfa5-f837-4395-b184-bfaea4f7e1ce"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The source and sink term for the plankton should correspond to its \
population growth and also its loss because it is consumed by the \
crustaceans.\n\nThe plankton population growth model could be unlimited \
growth, logistic limited growth, or another growth model.  For our case, \
consider a LOGISTIC growth model for the plankton source term:\n\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{" ", 
   RowBox[{"source", " ", "=", " ", 
    RowBox[{"r", "*", "\[Rho]", "*", 
     RowBox[{"(", " ", 
      RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
       FractionBox["\[Rho]", "k"]}], " ", ")"}], " "}]}]}]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"167fcd44-65b7-4e5d-9a70-041f0a690964"],
 "\n\nObserve that the above expression has a \"-\" (the book and the \
corresponding class presentation had a \"+\") (so that the plankton may NOT \
be autocatalytic).\nThe plankton sink term will correspond to the plankton \
being consumed by the crustaceans.  Consider a simple plankton-crustacean \
interaction model to be proportional to the plankton and crustacean \
densities:\n\n\tsink =  -  \[Alpha] \[Rho] h\n\nTherefore, the total source \
and sink term for the plankton is:\n\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"k1", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\[Rho]", ",", "h"}], "]"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"r", "*", "\[Rho]", "*", 
     RowBox[{"(", " ", 
      RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
       FractionBox["\[Rho]", "k"]}], " ", ")"}]}], " ", "-", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "*", "\[Rho]", "*", "h"}]}]}]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"56808fc4-c547-41ce-8e13-8e1c0d9ecb6b"],
 "\n"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"85f1cf5b-7de3-41be-87fd-24ffab825ba9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Using the notebook for this topic presented in class, perform the \
analysis using a logistic growth model for the plankton rather than the \
quadratic model presented in the book.  What if any differences in behavior \
do you observe?\n\nHint: ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "Make ",
 StyleBox["AccuracyGoal",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " smaller if needed to clean up the solution."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.4665339746953135`*^9, 
  3.466534017272621*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d252f2c3-d79d-49ea-a0ea-\
225170b8f52f"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\t5.8.17", "Section",
 FontSize->18,ExpressionUUID->"7ea81af6-3c05-466e-94c3-ed77c232cdcb"],

Cell["\<\
When you solve this problem, do it only one way.  Specifically, by finding \
the formula corresponding to the steady-state solution.  (Do not use numeric \
values for the constants that appear in the model).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"92919993-f91f-4502-8f53-fdfdd5d57c9c"],

Cell["\<\
Also, explicitly show that the homogeneous solutions are as specified in the \
book.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1119b95d-2338-4c42-b409-b8230defff66"]
}, Closed]]
}, Open  ]]
},
